IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `qld-part05-commencement`

-- Tests for Part 5 (qld-part05-commencement.l4).
-- Each expected value was worked out by hand from the text, as cited.

§ `Tests of Part 5`

§§ `ss 15 and 15C`

-- SAYS A reference to the enactment or passing of an Act is a reference to the fact of the Act's having received the royal assent, so an Act that has not received the royal assent is not enacted or passed in that sense (s 15).
#ASSERT `the Act is enacted or passed (s 15)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the Act is enacted or passed (s 15)` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `what a reference to the commencement of an Act is a reference to (s 15C(2))` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the commencement of the remaining provisions of the Act concerned`
#ASSERT `what a reference to the commencement of an Act is a reference to (s 15C(2))` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the commencement of the remaining provisions of the Act concerned`
#ASSERT `what a reference to the commencement of an Act is a reference to (s 15C(2))` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the commencement of the provision in which the reference is`
#ASSERT `what a reference to the commencement of an Act is a reference to (s 15C(2))` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the commencement of the relevant provision of the Act concerned`
#ASSERT `s 15C(1) applies to the Act despite anything in the Act (s 15C(3))` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 15C(1) applies to the Act despite anything in the Act (s 15C(3))` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a reference in s 15C to the provisions providing for citation includes the long title (s 15C(4))` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a reference in s 15C to the provisions providing for citation includes the long title (s 15C(4))` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `ss 15D to 15E`

#ASSERT `the way of fixing is open to the proclamation or other instrument (s 15D(1))` TRUE `a single day or time for the Act or the provisions` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the way of fixing is open to the proclamation or other instrument (s 15D(1))` TRUE `different days or times for different provisions` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the way of fixing is open to the proclamation or other instrument (s 15D(1))` TRUE `any other way` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the way of fixing is open to the proclamation or other instrument (s 15D(1))` FALSE `a single day or time for the Act or the provisions` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the proclamation is valid though the day or time fixed happens before the notification day (s 15D(2)(a))` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the proclamation is valid though the day or time fixed happens before the notification day (s 15D(2)(a))` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 15DA(1): the assent day is the date of assent of the Act, or of the Act that enacts the provision.
#ASSERT `the assent day (s 15DA(1))` TRUE (Date 5 4 1995) (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS Date 5 4 1995
#ASSERT `the assent day (s 15DA(1))` FALSE (Date 5 4 1995) (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS Date 1 1 2000
#ASSERT `the law is a postponed law (s 15DA(1), definition postponed law)` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the law is a postponed law (s 15DA(1), definition postponed law)` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the law is a postponed law (s 15DA(1), definition postponed law)` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the regulation extending the period may be made under the Act (s 15DA(4))` `the Act that is the postponed law` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the regulation extending the period may be made under the Act (s 15DA(4))` `the Act of which the postponed law is a provision` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the regulation extending the period may be made under the Act (s 15DA(4))` `an Act that the postponed law amends` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the regulation extending the period may be made under the Act (s 15DA(4))` `any other Act` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the amendment may be given a separate commencement (s 15E)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the amendment may be given a separate commencement (s 15E)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the amendment may be given a separate commencement (s 15E)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 17`

-- (1)(c): a power an empowering provision would confer may be exercised before the provision commences.
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised (s 17(1)(c))` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised (s 17(1)(c))` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the empowering provision commences on its enactment: s 17 does not answer
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised (s 17(1)(c))` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- exercised after commencement: s 17 does not answer
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised (s 17(1)(c))` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the empowering provision would confer no power and amend nothing
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised (s 17(1)(c))` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `anything may be done for the purpose of enabling the exercise of the power or bringing it into effect (s 17(1)(d))` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `anything may be done for the purpose of enabling the exercise of the power or bringing it into effect (s 17(1)(d))` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `anything may be done for the purpose of enabling the exercise of the power or bringing it into effect (s 17(1)(d))` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2)
#ASSERT `the basic and the additional instrument-making power may be exercised by making a single instrument (s 17(2)(c))` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the basic and the additional instrument-making power may be exercised by making a single instrument (s 17(2)(c))` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the provision of the instrument is treated as made under subsection (1) (s 17(2)(d))` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the provision of the instrument is treated as made under subsection (1) (s 17(2)(d))` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the provision of the instrument is treated as made under subsection (1) (s 17(2)(d))` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3): necessary instrument made on 10 March 2025, expressed to take effect on 20 March 2025: it takes effect on 20 March 2025.
-- SAYS An instrument made under s 17(1) that is necessary to enable the power to be exercised takes effect on its making, or on the later time at which it is expressed to take effect (s 17(3)).
#ASSERT `the day an instrument or provision necessary under s 17(3) takes effect (s 17(3))` (Date 10 3 2025) (JUST (Date 20 3 2025)) EQUALS Date 20 3 2025
#ASSERT `the day an instrument or provision necessary under s 17(3) takes effect (s 17(3))` (Date 10 3 2025) NOTHING EQUALS Date 10 3 2025
-- an expressed day that is not later than the making day: the making day applies (fork)
#ASSERT `the day an instrument or provision necessary under s 17(3) takes effect (s 17(3))` (Date 10 3 2025) (JUST (Date 5 3 2025)) EQUALS Date 10 3 2025
-- (4): an appointment takes effect on commencement of the relevant empowering provision (1 July 2025), or the later expressed time.
#ASSERT `the day an appointment, or an instrument or provision not necessary under s 17(3), takes effect (s 17(4))` (Date 1 7 2025) NOTHING EQUALS Date 1 7 2025
#ASSERT `the day an appointment, or an instrument or provision not necessary under s 17(3), takes effect (s 17(4))` (Date 1 7 2025) (JUST (Date 1 9 2025)) EQUALS Date 1 9 2025
#ASSERT `the day an appointment, or an instrument or provision not necessary under s 17(3), takes effect (s 17(4))` (Date 1 7 2025) (JUST (Date 1 6 2025)) EQUALS Date 1 7 2025
-- (5): before the empowering provision commences (1 July 2025), nothing done under (1) confers a right or imposes a liability.
-- SAYS Anything done under s 17(1) does not confer a right or impose a liability on a person before the relevant empowering provision commences (s 17(5)).
#ASSERT `anything done under s 17(1) confers a right or imposes a liability on a person on the day (s 17(5))` TRUE (Date 30 6 2025) (Date 1 7 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `anything done under s 17(1) confers a right or imposes a liability on a person on the day (s 17(5))` TRUE (Date 1 7 2025) (Date 1 7 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `anything done under s 17(1) confers a right or imposes a liability on a person on the day (s 17(5))` FALSE (Date 30 6 2025) (Date 1 7 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (6)
#ASSERT `the provision whose commencement subsections (1) and (4) refer to (s 17(6))` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the provision mentioned in subsection (1)(b) as amended by the empowering provision`
#ASSERT `the provision whose commencement subsections (1) and (4) refer to (s 17(6))` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the empowering provision`
#ASSERT `the provision whose commencement subsections (1) and (4) refer to (s 17(6))` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the empowering provision`
